    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed all failing tests in the frai-core suite. Here's what was broken and what I fixed:\n\n**Issue 1: Governance module missing named exports**\n- **Problem**: `src/finetune/governance.test.js` was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but `src/finetune/index.js` only exported it in the default export object.\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` at `src/finetune/index.js:363-366`.\n\n**Issue 2: Toxicity metric function signature mismatch**\n- **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was defined to accept `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metric functions with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be passed as banned terms, flagging legitimate outputs.\n- **Fix**: Updated the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` at `src/eval/metrics.js:56`, adding a guard to ensure only actual arrays of strings are used as banned terms.\n\n**Test Results:**\n- \u2705 All 28 tests pass\n- \u2705 All 8 test files pass\n- \u2705 All public exports preserved",
